3. Script and batch TikTok content & link shop
Batch creation: Plan themes for the next month (e.g., behind‑the‑scenes building of new digital packs, Hyperfocus ritual tips, success stories). Script and film 6–10 short videos in one or two sessions.

High‑energy storytelling: Use trending sounds and relevant hashtags (#ADHD, #Productivity, #Hyperfocus, #Planner2025). Keep videos 15‑60 seconds, open with a hook (e.g., “Struggling to focus? Here’s my secret weapon…”), and end with a CTA to your shop or Discord.

TikTok Shop integration: If not already, register for TikTok Shop. Add each Etsy product as a TikTok Shop item and tag it in your videos. Use TikTok’s “link in bio” to direct viewers to your Etsy store or a Linktree.

Monthly live sale: Schedule one TikTok Live per month featuring giveaways, Q&A with the Hyperfocus team, and limited‑time discounts. Promote lives on Discord and Patreon.

4. Create a Discord “Gig Marketplace”
Set up a dedicated channel (#hire-a-broski) in your Discord server.

Pin a gig template that members can copy–paste, with fields for task description, deliverables, payment (BROski$ or monetary), and contact method.

Build or modify your bot to accept gig submissions via a form command (e.g., /submit-gig). The bot can post the gig in the channel and DM the requester for details.

Reward system: When a gig is completed and approved, use your bot to award BROski$ automatically. Announce completions in a #celebrations channel.

Include marketplace rules in the channel description (e.g., no spam, clear deadlines, dispute resolution process). Encourage community members to post micro‑services such as copywriting, design, coding and technical support.

5. Outline & publish consulting/coaching packages
Package structure:

“Dopamine Overdrive” 1‑hour session – personalized ADHD workflow & productivity coaching.

“Ultra Agent Training” group workshop – teaches others how to build AI agents and use the Hyperfocus methodology.

“Creator Focus Accelerator” coaching bundle – monthly sessions with accountability check‑ins, digital templates and a private channel.

Pricing & booking: Set competitive prices (e.g., £99 for 1‑hour 1:1, £299 for group workshops) and include a discount for Patreon members. Use a scheduler like Calendly integrated with Stripe for payments and Discord for reminders.

Create landing pages: On your website or Notion, provide an overview of each package, deliverables, testimonials and FAQs. Embed booking widgets so clients can choose times.

Automate follow‑ups: After a booking, send a thank‑you email/DM with pre‑session questionnaires, call links, and resource downloads. Post‑session, send notes and a prompt to leave feedback. Use your bot to track completed coaching sessions and award BROski$ to participants.

Moving forward
These action plans give you clear steps to boost revenue across Patreon, Etsy, TikTok, community gigs and consulting. Since your operation is already gamified and heavily automated, integrate BROski$ rewards and celebration triggers into each new workflow. As you implement these tasks, celebrate each completion with a public shout‑out and a bonus BROski$ drop to maintain momentum.